        f"- **`wazigl v0.17.0-wazigl.6` vs Native `zig v0.17.1 -fllvm`**: Running the full LLVM 22 + Clang C++ toolchain inside Wasmtime (`wazigl.wasm`, `193.02 MiB`) incurs a ~2.2x–2.4x Wasmtime guest execution multiplier relative to native `zig -fllvm` (`{wl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` vs `{zl['compile_sec']['wasm_bench_runner_releasesmall']['warm']:.2f}s` warm on `ReleaseSmall`), making `wazig` ideal for fast CI test/check inner loops and `ReleaseFast +simd128` builds, and `wazigl` ideal when minimum `ReleaseSmall` wire size is desired without OS/arch-specific native compiler binaries.",
